# Faerie Fencing: "Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn. That creature gets an additional -3/-3 until end of turn if you
# controlled a Faerie as you cast this spell." Its ruling: "If you controlled a Faerie as you finished casting Faerie Fencing, it
# doesn't matter whether you still control one as the spell resolves." Bot1 controls Faerie Mastermind as it casts Faerie Fencing
# with X = 1 at Bot2's Concealing Curtains (0/4) on Bot2's turn; Bot2 answers by killing the Mastermind with Lightning Bolt, so
# Bot1 controls no Faerie as Fencing resolves (checked with Fencing still on the stack). The Curtains still get -1/-1 and -3/-3:
# 0 toughness, into the graveyard (CR 601.2i, 704.5f). Read as it resolves it would be -1/3 and live.

